# Gate step 1059-ry6t — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# First binding I have written as a data file rather than as an inline block in
# build.sh, and it is the direct payoff of esme's migration: two of the seven
# near-drops that motivated the freeze were my steps landing into that shared
# region. Prefix 055 sits between 050 and 060 on the ten-spacing, so nothing is
# renamed and this file conflicts with nothing.
#
# WHAT THE FIXTURE PINS. crates/tillandsias-windows-tray/build.rs writes an
# EMPTY placeholder for the musl headless when it is absent, so include_bytes!
# compiles on a host that will never package. That accommodation is deliberate
# and it is the same one render_msix_logos makes for the MSIX logos — whose
# comment already states the rule this asset never got: "the packaging step is
# where absence becomes an error, because that is where it actually matters."
#
# So the documented local build printed `Built: …`, exited 0, and produced a
# tray whose guest injection was a SILENT NO-OP. It does not fail at build; it
# fails later, in a guest that behaves like an older release for no visible
# reason — the kind of symptom this fleet then spends a night bisecting.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-05: 0 bytes on esmeraldinha since 2026-08-23 and on yolanda
# since 2026-08-22, TWO OF TWO Windows hosts checked. build.rs creates the
# placeholder on first build and nothing replaces it, so this was the DEFAULT
# state of a Windows dev checkout, not one stale machine. That answers the
# question the packet deliberately left open.
#
# The split follows the logos precedent rather than inventing one: build.rs
# WARNS (refusing there would break the `cargo check` accommodation), and
# scripts/build-windows-tray.ps1 REFUSES, because that script's whole purpose is
# to produce an installable tray.
STEP_DESC="Checking a placeholder guest asset cannot build a silent no-op tray (1059-ry6t)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-tray-asset-placeholder-refused.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the windows-tray build no longer warns or refuses on a zero-byte embedded guest binary (1059-ry6t) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Tray guest-asset placeholder check passed"
